This photo shows leftovers: an orange sauce residue on one plate, a yellow mashed or scrambled residue on another, an almost clean small plate, and a nearly empty bowl. Only small remnants of food are left.

I estimated about 10 g of orange residue at about 1.5 kcal/g (about 15 kcal), about 15 g of yellow residue at about 1.5 kcal/g (about 22 kcal), and about 2 g of crumbs on the other two dishes (about 3 kcal). That gives roughly 40 kcal over about 27 g, which I rounded to 28 g.

